<reference id="tpu7x-configurations" xml:lang="en-US">
  <title><keyword keyref="product-tpu7x"/> supported configurations</title>
  <shortdesc>The slice shapes you can request for <keyword keyref="product-tpu7x"/>, and how many chips and hosts each uses.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <author type="contributor">Siddharth Rao (adaptation)</author>
    <copyright><copyryear year="2026"/><copyrholder>Google LLC (source content, CC BY 4.0)</copyrholder></copyright>
    <critdates><created date="2026-10-24"/><revised modified="2026-10-22"/></critdates>
    <metadata><audience type="ml-engineer"/></metadata>
    <data name="source" value="tpu7x" href="https://docs.cloud.google.com/tpu/docs/tpu7x" format="html" scope="external"/>
    <data name="licence" value="CC BY 4.0. Adapted from the source page and modified: restructured as DITA, values moved to keys."/>
    
  </prolog>
  <refbody>
    <section id="slice-shapes">
      <title>Slice shapes</title>
      <note conref="../reuse/tpu-warehouse.dita#tpu-warehouse/note-slice-shape"/>
      <table outputclass="slice-shapes"><tgroup cols="6"><colspec colname="c1"/><colspec colname="c2"/><colspec colname="c3"/><colspec colname="c4"/><colspec colname="c5"/><colspec colname="c6"/><thead><row><entry>Shape</entry><entry>Chips</entry><entry>Hosts</entry><entry>VMs</entry><entry>Cubes</entry><entry>Scope</entry></row></thead><tbody>
<row><entry>2x2x1</entry><entry>4</entry><entry>1</entry><entry>1</entry><entry>1/16</entry><entry>Single-host</entry></row>
<row><entry>2x2x2</entry><entry>8</entry><entry>2</entry><entry>2</entry><entry>1/8</entry><entry>Multi-host</entry></row>
<row><entry>2x2x4</entry><entry>16</entry><entry>4</entry><entry>4</entry><entry>1/4</entry><entry>Multi-host</entry></row>
<row><entry>2x4x4</entry><entry>32</entry><entry>8</entry><entry>8</entry><entry>1/2</entry><entry>Multi-host</entry></row>
<row><entry>4x4x4</entry><entry>64</entry><entry>16</entry><entry>16</entry><entry>1</entry><entry>Multi-host</entry></row>
<row><entry>4x4x8</entry><entry>128</entry><entry>32</entry><entry>32</entry><entry>2</entry><entry>Multi-host</entry></row>
<row><entry>4x8x8</entry><entry>256</entry><entry>64</entry><entry>64</entry><entry>4</entry><entry>Multi-host</entry></row>
<row><entry>8x8x8</entry><entry>512</entry><entry>128</entry><entry>128</entry><entry>8</entry><entry>Multi-host</entry></row>
<row><entry>8x8x16</entry><entry>1024</entry><entry>256</entry><entry>256</entry><entry>16</entry><entry>Multi-host</entry></row>
<row><entry>8x16x16</entry><entry>2048</entry><entry>512</entry><entry>512</entry><entry>32</entry><entry>Multi-host</entry></row>
</tbody></tgroup></table>
      <p>Shapes also follow the general form <codeph>AxBxC</codeph>, where each dimension is a multiple of 4, up to <keyword keyref="tpu7x-chips-per-pod"/> chips. Every shape uses the <keyword keyref="tpu7x-machine-type"/> machine type. Slices larger than <keyword keyref="tpu7x-max-api-slice"/> chips require contacting your account team.</p>
    </section>
  </refbody>
</reference>
